                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "colette":</h3><p>Schoeps&#8217; &#8220;Colette&#8221; series is a modular small-diaphragm microphone system comprised of 20 different capsule designs and numerous head amps, both analog and digital. </p><p>Most polar patterns are available in either end-address or side-address designs. Additionally, many special-purpose capsules, incorporating fixed EQ settings, allow use in otherwise challenging applications. </p><p>Optional inline &#8220;active accessories,&#8221; fitted between capsule and head amplifier, include an attenuator, swivel, high-pass filter, and a series of extension tubes and cables to facilitate positioning.</p><p>The capsules in the Colette series have part numbers beginning with <b>MK</b>, such as the MK 4 Cardioid end-address capsule. The head amplifiers use part numbers beginning with <b>CMC</b>, such as the CMC 6 solid-state, low-noise, low-impedance &#8220;microphone amplifier.&#8221;</p><p>The series was introduced in 1973.</p>
